    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d221">

                <pb facs="0380" n="288" xml:id="pg288"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/1800</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stovall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-15T13:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 15, 1918, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 16, 8.22 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3958. My 3884.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d221-f1"/> In conversation with a member of
                    French Embassy, latter states that De Fiori, “a dangerous
                    agent of Ludendorff,” was in
                    Switzerland endeavoring to get into touch with Entente and especially America.
                    It is possible that this was said to sound out the Legation. Merely to avoid any
                    misunderstanding, I shall be glad to have the Department’s permission to
                    acquaint British, French and Italian colleagues with substance of De
                        Fiori’s communications without revealing channel through which
                        received.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d221-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stovall</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d221-f1" n="1" xml:id="d221-f1-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg276">p. 276</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d221-f2" n="2" xml:id="d221-f2-content">
                <p>Answered by telegram No. 2313, July 19, 5 p.m., “Department has no objection to
                    your informing British, French and Italian colleagues as you suggest.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
